      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Warm wilderness and deserts",
            "Subterranean areas, underground burrows, and dungeons"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A five- to six-foot scorpion with a hard green carapace, yellowish green legs and pincers, and a segmented black tail ending in a stinger."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Attack options",
          "lines": [
            "Two pincers and one sting. The attacks can target up to three opponents."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Pincer grab · Each pincer deals 1d10 damage. A grabbed victim takes another 1d10 each round until released. The victim gets one bend bars/lift gates attempt per combat as their sole action for that round.",
            "Sting · The sting deals 1d4 damage. It automatically hits a victim caught in the pincers if directed at that victim. Roll normally against an untrapped target. A failed save vs. type F poison kills the victim the next round.",
            "Stinging frenzy · At 1 or 2 HP, the Giant Scorpion makes two tail-only sting attempts per round. The entry states that scorpions can be affected by their own poison.",
            "Aggression · It has a 95% chance to attack any creature that approaches."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Lair mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Burrow · An underground burrow or dungeon lair has a 20% chance to contain 5d4 eggs."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "1–4 appearing. Uncommon. The table lists swarm organization, any activity, carnivore, no intelligence (0), treasure D, and neutral alignment.",
            "Steady (11) morale. Special defenses and magic resistance Nil.",
            "This creature entry specifies death next round on a failed Type F save. The Dungeon Master Guide general poison table lists immediate onset.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, p. 309."
          ]
        }
      ],
